6.7 Phylogeny
The SILVA ACT guide tree for this job contains only our isolates (no SILVA reference sequences). For the phylogeny below we root the tree on an isolate classified as Lactococcus (Bacillota, the most basal phylum recovered).


Show/hide code
tree &lt;- ape::read.tree(silva_tree_file)

outgroup_tip &lt;- classified |&gt;
  filter(genus == outgroup_genus, seq_id %in% tree$tip.label) |&gt;
  pull(seq_id) |&gt;
  pluck(1)

tree_rooted &lt;- ape::root(tree, outgroup = outgroup_tip, resolve.root = TRUE)

isolate_tips &lt;- intersect(tree_rooted$tip.label, classified$seq_id)
tree_pruned &lt;- ape::keep.tip(tree_rooted, isolate_tips)


Every family recovered among the tree’s isolates gets its own tip color below — nothing is pooled into an “Other” category. Isolates with a domain-level SILVA classification but no resolved family are labeled “Unclassified”.


Show/hide code
all_family_tree &lt;- classified |&gt;
  filter(seq_id %in% isolate_tips, !is.na(family)) |&gt;
  distinct(family) |&gt;
  arrange(family) |&gt;
  pull(family)

family_tree_pal &lt;- make_palette(all_family_tree)

tip_data &lt;- assemblies |&gt;
  filter(seq_id %in% isolate_tips) |&gt;
  select(seq_id) |&gt;
  left_join(
    classified |&gt; select(seq_id, family),
    by = "seq_id"
  ) |&gt;
  transmute(
    label = seq_id,
    seq_id,
    family_grp = coalesce(family, "Unclassified")
  )




Show/hide code
ggtree(tree_pruned, layout = "rectangular") %&lt;+%
  tip_data +
  geom_tippoint(aes(color = family_grp), size = 1.5) +
  geom_tiplab(aes(label = seq_id), size = 2, hjust = -0.1) +
  scale_color_manual(
    values = c(family_tree_pal, "Unclassified" = "grey50"),
    name = "Family"
  ) +
  guides(color = guide_legend(ncol = 1, override.aes = list(size = 3))) +
  geom_treescale(offset = 1)








Figure 9: Phylogeny of the 170 classified isolates, rooted on an isolate classified as Lactococcus. Tip points are colored by family, with every family recovered (15) shown individually; isolates with a domain-level SILVA classification but no resolved family are labeled “Unclassified”. Scale bar represents substitutions per site.
